{"name":"Audrey’s Blush","hex":"#ae8087","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of blushing; a pink or red glow on the face caused by embarrassment, shame, shyness, love, etc.","A glow; a flush of colour, especially pink or red."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become red or pink in the face (and sometimes experience an associated feeling of warmth), especially due to shyness, love, shame, excitement, or embarrassment.","To be shy, ashamed, or embarrassed (to do something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Audrey","blocks":[{"text":"Audrey is a feminine given name. It is rarely a masculine given name. Audrey is the Anglo-Norman form of the Anglo-Saxon name Æðelþryð, composed of the elements æðel \"noble\" and þryð \"strength\". The literal definition of the word is “noble strength” or “strength from nobility”. The Anglo-Norman form of the name was applied to Saint Audrey, also known by the historical form of her name as Saint Æthelthryth. The same name also survived into the modern period in its Anglo-Saxon form, as Etheldred, e.g. Etheldred Benett (1776–1845) and Etheldred Browning (1869–1946)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/St-aethelthryth.jpg/330px-St-aethelthryth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audrey","wikidata":"Q2639295"},{"title":"Blush (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Blush is a medium bright tone of pink."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Blush_rose_1.jpg/330px-Blush_rose_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blush_(color)","wikidata":"Q22133966"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"blush":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/97/En-us-blush.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/97/En-us-blush.ogg/En-us-blush.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Fishing Boats on the Beach by Anton Mauve Rijksdienst voor het Cultureel Erfgoed B918","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Fishing_Boats_on_the_Beach_by_Anton_Mauve_Rijksdienst_voor_het_Cultureel_Erfgoed_B918.jpg/500px-Fishing_Boats_on_the_Beach_by_Anton_Mauve_Rijksdienst_voor_het_Cultureel_Erfgoed_B918.jpg","ratio":1.424962852897474,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fishing_Boats_on_the_Beach_by_Anton_Mauve_Rijksdienst_voor_het_Cultureel_Erfgoed_B918.jpg","share":0.074375},{"title":"Anton Mauve - Schapenkudde","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Anton_Mauve_-_Schapenkudde.jpg/500px-Anton_Mauve_-_Schapenkudde.jpg","ratio":1.5645371577574967,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Mauve_-_Schapenkudde.jpg","share":0.071875},{"title":"Mauve surprise and Rosebud (Fabergé eggs)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Mauve_surprise_and_Rosebud_%28Faberg%C3%A9_eggs%29.jpg/500px-Mauve_surprise_and_Rosebud_%28Faberg%C3%A9_eggs%29.jpg","ratio":1.5003663003663004,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mauve_surprise_and_Rosebud_(Faberg%C3%A9_eggs).jpg","share":0.059375},{"title":"Suit, woman's, two-piece (AM 1995.78.1-4)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Suit%2C_woman%27s%2C_two-piece_%28AM_1995.78.1-4%29.jpg/500px-Suit%2C_woman%27s%2C_two-piece_%28AM_1995.78.1-4%29.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suit,_woman%27s,_two-piece_(AM_1995.78.1-4).jpg","share":0.044375},{"title":"Barberini August 2023-Anton Mauve - In Scheveningen,1876 - De Mesdag Collectie, Den Haag-3","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Barberini_August_2023-Anton_Mauve_-_In_Scheveningen%2C1876_-_De